   ("Match your business name", "Your domain should match your business name as closely as possible. If the exact .com is taken, a different extension (.co, .io, .shop) is usually better than adding words like \"get\" or \"the\", although short prefixes such as get or try are common for apps."),
   ("Avoid hyphens and numbers", "Hyphens are easy to forget and numbers are confusing when spoken (is it 4 or four?). Both make your domain harder to share by word of mouth."),
   ("Pick the right extension", ".com is still the most trusted choice for customers. .co is popular with startups, .io with tech companies, .app with apps and .shop with online stores. Choose the one your customers will remember."),
